Story: Boil when the power is cheap
  Approval: approved
  As a tea drinker
  I want the kettle to boil when electricity is cheap
  So that my morning cup costs less without me watching the price

  You make tea every morning and your power is cheaper at some hours. Instead of checking
  the price, you ask for a cheap boil. This tutorial also shows what happens when the price
  provider goes quiet, because that is when you most need to know what the kettle is doing.

  Scenario: Ask for a cheap boil, lose the provider, get the boil
    When the user asks for a cheap boil
    Then the cheap boil is waiting
    When the feed stops answering
    Then the price feed is unavailable
    And the cheap boil is waiting
    When the feed answers again
    Then the price feed is live
    When the price drops to the cheap rate
    Then the cheap boil is boiling

Story: Knowing how far to trust the price
  Approval: approved
  As a tea drinker
  I want to see when the price is old
  So that I do not wait for, or rely on, a price that has already changed

  The dot next to the price tells you how current it is. This tutorial follows a price from
  live to late to missing, and shows what each state means for you.

  Scenario: A price goes late, then missing, then returns
    When the feed falls behind
    Then the price feed is delayed
    When the feed stops answering
    Then the price feed is unavailable
    When the feed answers again
    Then the price feed is live

Story: A cheap boil on a late price
  Approval: proposed
  As a tea drinker
  I want the kettle to boil even when the price is late
  So that I do not miss a cheap hour

  Whether a late price may start a boil is not decided yet (see the boiling when it is cheap
  topic), so this tutorial is proposed and is left out of the approved manual.

  Scenario: A late price reaches the cheap rate
    When the user asks for a cheap boil
    Then the cheap boil is waiting
    When the feed falls behind
    Then the price feed is delayed
    When the price drops to the cheap rate
    Then the cheap boil is boiling
